content:
Put into it the pieces of meat,
    all the choice pieces—the leg and the shoulder.
  Fill it with the best of these bones;

It has frustrated all efforts;
    its heavy deposit has not been removed,
    not even by fire.

The merchants among the nations scoff at you;
    you have come to a horrible end
    and will be no more.’ ”

Men of Arvad and Helek
    guarded your walls on every side;
  men of Gammad
    were in your towers.
  They hung their shields around your walls;
    they brought your beauty to perfection.

I will set fire to Egypt;
    Pelusium will writhe in agony.
  Thebes will be taken by storm;
    Memphis will be in constant distress.

All the shining lights in the heavens
    I will darken over you;
    I will bring darkness over your land, declares the Sovereign Lord.

Outside is the sword;
    inside are plague and famine.
  Those in the country
    will die by the sword;
  those in the city
    will be devoured by famine and plague.
